<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Next dose.

     REWRITTEN 20 Oct 2026, and the header used to be wrong about the most
     important thing on the card. It said "HERE THE COUNTDOWN IS IN THE
     CENTRE", which was true of the layout and false of the widget: the
     countdown could not fit in the ring's hole at any legible size, so the
     provider put a status WORD there instead, and the number the owner wanted
     to see - the time - was nowhere.

     What the card shows now, and why:

       - the ring's centre carries the LIVE COUNTDOWN, ticking in the launcher
         process with no app running ("6:18:35"), because the ring is the
         live thing and the owner asked for the countdown to be in it;
       - the MEDICATION NAME sits directly under the ring, because the name is
         what the dose is FOR (the owner's order, 21 Oct);
       - the FIXED TIME ("4:00am") sits under that, because the time it
         counts down to does not change and reads as the answer to "when?";
       - in the DUE and OVERDUE states the ring carries the word DUE and the
         fixed-time line carries the state instead ("Due now").

     The ring is 50dp with a 4dp stroke, so the hole is 42dp - which is what
     the countdown needs: the platform's whole-duration format measures 100px
     at 12sp on this device, and it does not fit an 88px hole.

     FrameLayout root, for the L-076 reason recorded in doxy_pep_widget.xml: one
     ViewGroup, children positioned with layout_gravity, no nesting. The bands
     do not have to sum to the widget height, so an overflowing eyebrow or a long
     medication name cannot push content off either end - which is exactly the
     defect that clipped this layout in the audit.

     The medication name has autosize rather than a fit() call. Once
     autoSizeTextType is on, TextView.setTextSize is a no-op (the framework guards
     it with !isAutoSizeEnabled()), so WidgetTextFit cannot shrink it and would
     only log a decision that never happened. It needs match_parent for the
     measure to be EXACTLY constrained, and gravity=center to keep looking
     centred once the view is full-width. The whole reason autosize works in
     RemoteViews at all is recorded in CLAUDE.md. -->
<FrameLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:id="@+id/widget_root"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:padding="16dp"
    android:background="@drawable/widget_background">

    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_title"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_gravity="top|start"
         android:text="Next dose"
         android:textSize="16sp"
         android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary"
         android:textStyle="bold"
        android:maxLines="2"
        android:breakStrategy="simple" />

    <!-- 50dp, moved UP to 26dp from the top of the card.
         The owner asked for both (20 Oct): the ring was "oversized" AND it
         left a band of dead space between the title and the ring. Moving it up
         closes that band, and growing it gives the countdown room - the
         platform's format ("6:18:35") measures 100px at 12sp on this device,
         which needs a 42dp hole to sit in with air around it.

         The drawable is innerRadius 21dp + thickness 4dp, so the hole is
         exactly 42dp and the drawable and the view are the same size - a shape
         drawable is drawn at its own size and CLIPPED if the view is smaller. -->
    <ProgressBar
        android:id="@+id/widget_ring"
        style="@style/ShosWidgetRing"
        android:layout_width="50dp"
        android:layout_height="50dp"
        android:layout_gravity="top|center_horizontal"
        android:layout_marginTop="26dp"
        android:rotation="-90"
        android:max="100" />

    <!-- THE COUNTDOWN IS IN THE RING.

         It is a real Chronometer, so it ticks in the launcher process with no
         app running, no alarm and no wake lock. The platform's format is the
         whole duration - "6:18:35" - because RemoteViews.setChronometer's
         format argument is a single-string template with one %s and the
         components cannot be selected; the owner said seconds are the least
         important part, which is what makes a seven-character number
         acceptable in the hole.

         The width is FIXED and equal to the ring's hole, which is what makes
         the autosize work: autoSize measures the view's own width, so a
         wrap_content view would measure its own text and could never shrink
         it. The marginTop puts it in the RING, not in the middle of the
         card: the ring sits 26dp from the top and is 50dp across, so its hole
         is centred on 51dp, and 43dp is where a one-line 12sp number has to
         start to sit on that centre. -->
    <Chronometer
        android:id="@+id/widget_countdown"
        android:layout_width="42dp"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_gravity="top|center_horizontal"
        android:layout_marginTop="43dp"
        android:gravity="center"
        android:textSize="12sp"
        android:textStyle="bold"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary"
        android:maxLines="1"
        android:autoSizeTextType="uniform"
        android:autoSizeMaxTextSize="12sp"
        android:autoSizeMinTextSize="9sp"
        android:autoSizeStepGranularity="1sp"
        android:clickable="false"
        android:focusable="false" />

    <!-- The status word, also in the ring's centre, for the two states where
         there is no countdown to show: DUE (a dose is due now) and OVERDUE.
         A Chronometer can render a static string - a format with no %s in it
         is used literally - but the two are different view types, so the
         provider shows one and hides the other. -->
    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_ring_label"
        android:layout_width="42dp"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_gravity="top|center_horizontal"
        android:layout_marginTop="43dp"
        android:gravity="center"
        android:text=""
        android:textSize="12sp"
        android:textStyle="bold"
        android:maxLines="1"
        android:autoSizeTextType="uniform"
        android:autoSizeMaxTextSize="12sp"
        android:autoSizeMinTextSize="9sp"
        android:autoSizeStepGranularity="1sp" />

    <!-- The medication the time belongs to, directly under the ring: the name
         is what the dose is FOR, and the time is when.

         The JS sends now sends EVERY medication with a dose pending, by name
         (the owner: "next dose, if space list all meds not just +2"), so
         this line can be two lines: "Sertraline, PrEP, Vitamin D" is twenty-
         eight characters, and the card's text is 76.7dp - about fourteen
         characters a line at 11sp. The autosize steps the text down until it
         fits in two lines, and the widest word is what it measures, so the
         names break at their spaces rather than mid-word.

         THE HEIGHT IS FIXED, and that is the part that makes the autosize
         work. With a wrap_content height the view's height is the text's
         own height, so the framework has no height to fit the text INTO: it
         settled on 13sp and three lines, and the third was clipped by
         maxLines. A fixed two-line height gives it the box to fit.

         The count of the later doses is gone: a count says how many and not
         which, and the owner's own rule is that anything which will alert
         must be visible on this widget. -->
    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_med_name"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="30dp"
        android:layout_gravity="top|center_horizontal"
        android:layout_marginTop="80dp"
        android:gravity="center"
        android:text="Medication"
        android:textSize="12sp"
        android:textStyle="bold"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_text_primary"
        android:maxLines="2"
        android:breakStrategy="simple"
        android:autoSizeTextType="uniform"
        android:autoSizeMaxTextSize="12sp"
        android:autoSizeMinTextSize="9sp"
        android:autoSizeStepGranularity="1sp" />

    <!-- The FIXED TIME, under the name: "4:00am" is when the dose is due, and
         it does not change, so it is the caption under the ring rather than the
         number inside it. In the DUE and OVERDUE states this line carries the
         state instead ("Due now").

         It is at 110dp because the names above it can be two lines: 80dp plus
         two lines of 11sp is 108dp, and the card is 134dp tall. -->
    <TextView
        android:id="@+id/widget_next_dose"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_gravity="top|center_horizontal"
        android:layout_marginTop="112dp"
        android:text="--:--"
        android:textSize="12sp"
        android:textColor="@color/widget_text_muted"
        android:maxLines="2"
        android:breakStrategy="simple" />
</FrameLayout>
